//!
//! # Apic
//!
//! The local APIC and the IOAPIC: the interrupt controllers that replace the
//! 8259 on every modern x86_64 machine.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name           | File          | Purpose                                                  |
//! |----------------|---------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Apic::Lapic`  | `lapic.ign`   | the per-processor controller: enable, EOI, timer         |
//! | `Apic::Ioapic` | `ioapic.ign`  | the device-side controller: routes a GSI to a vector     |
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! | Imports | Why                                                                  |
//! |---------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Arch`  | MSR access for `IA32_APIC_BASE`                                      |
//! | `Mm`    | `Mm::Vmm::map` maps the uncached register pages                      |
//! | `Acpi`  | the MADT says where the IOAPICs are and how the ISA IRQs are wired   |
//!
//! These files would belong in `Arch` if they did not need the memory manager
//! and ACPI. `Arch` is a leaf, so they form their own subsystem. `Time` and
//! `Trap` import `Apic`.

import _ from "./ioapic";
import _ from "./lapic";

/// Aggregate namespace of the interrupt controllers. The files above
/// contribute `Apic::Lapic` and `Apic::Ioapic`.
export namespace Apic {}
